<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Stack Overflow Developer Survey — published marts</title>
  <style>
    :root { --ink: #1a1a1a; --muted: #555; --line: #d8d8d8; --bar: #2c5f8a; --bg: #fafafa; --card: #fff; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body { margin: 0; font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; color: var(--ink); background: var(--bg); line-height: 1.45; }
    header, main { max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 0; }
    header { padding-bottom: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 1.6rem 0 0.5rem; }
    h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 1rem 0 0.4rem; }
    .as-of { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--muted); }
    .lede { font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .panel { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; margin: 0.6rem 0 1rem; }
    .panel dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 11rem 1fr; gap: 0.2rem 0.8rem; margin: 0; }
    .panel dt { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
    .panel dd { margin: 0; font-family: ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .badge { display: inline-block; background: #f3e6c8; color: #5a3d00; font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 3px; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
    .not-asked { margin: 0.35rem 0; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .empty, .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
    svg.chart { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 0.4rem 0 0.8rem; }
    .bar-label, .bar-num { font-size: 11px; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; fill: var(--ink); }
    .bar { fill: var(--bar); }
    pre.contract { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 0.78rem; background: #f3f3f3; padding: 0.75rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); font-family: ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace; }
    footer { max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 2rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
    code { font-family: ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  </style>
</head>
<body data-published-years="{{ year_list | join(',') }}">
  <header>
    <h1>Stack Overflow Developer Survey — published results</h1>
    <p class="as-of" data-as-of="{{ data_as_of }}">Data as of {{ data_as_of }}. This page is regenerated from the warehouse after each successful publish. It is not a live query.</p>
    <p class="lede">Numbers below come from <code>marts.v_salary_analytics</code>, <code>marts.v_tech_adoption</code>, and <code>marts.v_ai_sentiment</code> — the same views that filter to <code>dwh.active_release</code>. They are not read from the historical <code>marts.mart_*</code> tables.</p>
  </header>
  <main>
    {% if nothing_published %}
    <p class="empty">Nothing is published yet. <code>dwh.active_release</code> is empty, so the views have no rows.</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% for y in years %}
    <section class="panel" data-provenance-year="{{ y.survey_year }}">
      <h2>{{ y.survey_year }} release</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>active release_id</dt>
        <dd><code data-release-id="{{ y.release_id }}">{{ y.release_id_short }}</code> (full: {{ y.release_id }})</dd>
        <dt>published_at</dt>
        <dd>{{ y.published_at_label }}</dd>
        <dt>salary-cell respondents</dt>
        <dd data-salary-respondents="{{ y.salary_cell_respondents }}">{{ y.salary_cell_respondents }} people in published salary cells ({{ y.salary_n_cells }} {{ 'cell' if y.salary_n_cells == 1 else 'cells' }}). This is <em>not</em> the raw survey headcount — salary filters and HAVING ≥ 5 apply. See the contract excerpt below.</dd>
        <dt>AI-cell respondents</dt>
        <dd data-ai-respondents="{{ y.ai_cell_respondents }}">{{ y.ai_cell_respondents }} people in published AI cells ({{ y.ai_n_cells }} {{ 'cell' if y.ai_n_cells == 1 else 'cells' }}).</dd>
        <dt>tech rows</dt>
        <dd>{{ y.tech_n_cells }} language/database {{ 'row' if y.tech_n_cells == 1 else 'rows' }} that passed the ≥ 100-user cutoff.</dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <h3>{{ y.survey_year }} — salary (median, mixed local currencies)</h3>
    {{ y.salary_svg | safe }}

    <h3>{{ y.survey_year }} — technology adoption (languages, top 10)</h3>
    {{ y.tech_svg | safe }}

    <h3>{{ y.survey_year }} — share who see AI as a threat</h3>
    {{ y.ai_threat_svg | safe }}

    <h3>{{ y.survey_year }} — average job satisfaction</h3>
    {{ y.ai_job_svg | safe }}
    {% endfor %}

    <section id="year-over-year" data-yoy="{{ 'true' if yoy.enabled else 'false' }}">
      <h2>Year-over-year</h2>
      {% if not yoy.enabled %}
      <p class="note">Year-over-year charts appear when two or more survey years are published. Only {{ year_list | join(' and ') or 'no years' }} {{ 'is' if year_list|length == 1 else 'are' }} live in <code>dwh.active_release</code>, so this section does not invent a second year.</p>
      {% else %}
        <h3>Salary cells present in more than one year</h3>
        {% if yoy.salary_empty %}
        <p class="note">No overlapping salary cells across the published years (same country, band, role, remote, org size). The page does not compare unrelated cells.</p>
        {% endif %}
        {% for block in yoy.salary %}
        <p>{{ block.label }}</p>
        {{ block.svg | safe }}
        {% endfor %}

        <h3>Technologies present in more than one year</h3>
        {% if yoy.tech_empty %}
        <p class="note">No overlapping technologies across the published years.</p>
        {% endif %}
        {% for block in yoy.tech %}
        <p>{{ block.label }}</p>
        {{ block.svg | safe }}
        {% endfor %}

        <h3>AI threat rate for answer groups present in more than one year</h3>
        {% if yoy.ai_empty %}
        <p class="note">No overlapping AI answer groups across the published years.</p>
        {% endif %}
        {% for block in yoy.ai %}
        <p>{{ block.label }}</p>
        {{ block.svg | safe }}
        {% endfor %}
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    <h2>What these numbers are (from data_contracts.md)</h2>
    <p class="note">The blocks below are copied from <code>docs/data_contracts.md</code>, not rewritten here.</p>
    <h3>Compensation</h3>
    <pre class="contract" data-contract="currency">{{ contracts.currency }}</pre>
    <h3>Salary mart</h3>
    <pre class="contract" data-contract="salary">{{ contracts.salary }}</pre>
    <h3>Tech mart</h3>
    <pre class="contract" data-contract="tech">{{ contracts.tech }}</pre>
    <h3>AI mart</h3>
    <pre class="contract" data-contract="ai">{{ contracts.ai }}</pre>
  </main>
  <footer>
    Generated by <code>scripts/render_dashboard.py</code>. Charts are inline SVG computed in Python; there is no Chart.js and no CDN.
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
